feat: Add Euclidean distance and enhance RAG similarity validation

Context:
This change introduces Euclidean distance as a new option for similarity/distance calculations in the RAG pipeline and improves the embedding similarity validation tool.

Changes made:
- Added Euclidean distance function to mathUtils.ts and integrated it into calculateSimilarity.
- Updated ClusteredSearchService.ts and RAGManager.ts to support Euclidean distance for context retrieval, including correct sorting logic (lower is better).
- Added 'Euclidean Distance' to the similarity metric selection dropdown in rag-test.astro for both the main RAG pipeline and the embedding similarity validation section.
- Refactored the worker-side embedding similarity validation (performSimilarityValidation in rag_worker.ts) to use its own dedicated feature-extraction pipeline (Snowflake/snowflake-arctic-embed-xs model).
- Corrected various initialization checks and fixed reference errors in rag_test_main.ts and rag_worker.ts related to these changes.

Impact:
Provides more flexibility in choosing similarity metrics for RAG, potentially improving retrieval relevance for different types of queries or embedding models. Enhances the diagnostic capabilities of the similarity validation tool by allowing metric selection and ensuring correct model usage for comparison. 